==Changelog - March 26th==
{{Collapsed section|18|CLICK HERE TO SHOW}}
'''Poll 83 Changes'''

* Updated the Slayer Cape perk when used at Konar to reassign tasks within the same area. The perk now considers the specific location of the task when offering a repeat assignment.
* You can now cast Alchemy by using items on the Explorer’s Ring, removing the need to wear it or navigate a dialogue box.
* Added a new dialogue option to receive another farming contract at the same tier as the one a player has just completed.
* You can now mouse over any fairy ring you have unlocked on the world map to be reminded of its code.
* Added a seed pack reward to Tithe Farm in exchange for points.
* Prayer tooltips now shows the base drain rates of all prayers.
* Updated the Shades of Morton's chest designs with clearer markings on top, making them more distinguishable.
* ​Mazchna, Vannaka, and Chaeldar now assign Slayer tasks to hunt Crabs. This includes Ammonite, Frost, Rock, Sand and Swamp crabs.
* All skill guides now feature a new tab named after the skill, providing an overview of what the skill is and the benefits of levelling it.
* Your game settings will now be automatically adjusted based on your choice when asked on Tutorial Island whether you’re a Beginner, Returning, or Experienced player.

'''Player Support Update'''

* From today onwards, whenever your macroing (botting) report has been reviewed and actioned, you'll receive an inbox message directly in your Message Centre.

'''Emote Looping Continued'''

* The emote looping feature has been added to an additional 45 emotes. This also includes looping for specific treasure trail items such as Flared trousers, Sleeping cap, Powdered wig and Pantaloons.

'''W345 Permanent Deadman Changes'''

* Increased the rarity of Charms and stopped players with Deadman protection from obtaining them. This is to help the prices of the items long term and reward players taking those risks with extra loot!
* Removed the Elite Diary requirement for purchasing Elite Void. Now you can simply take a regular Void Knight Top or Void Knight Robes to the Elite Void Knight at Pest Control and upgrade your regular void pieces to Elite void pieces for 200 points per piece!
* Added an option to change the respawn location to the Grand Exchange. Talk to Brugsen Bursen at the Grand Exchange to choose your respawn point upon death, similar to Deadman Armageddon.
* All players can now use Chivalry, Rigour, and Augury in Permanent Deadman Mode provided they have the prayer level requirement, regardless of their defence level. Chivalry still requires the completion of the Holy Grail quest, Rigour and Augury still requires the prayer scrolls.
* Trinkets now turn to Trinket dust upon death, similar to Charms.
* The old Deadman skulls (as seen in Bounty Hunter) have returned to Permanent Deadman.
* A check has been added to prevent skulled players from diving with the rowboat on Fossil Island.

'''Other Changes'''

* Logging out whilst in the Theatre of Blood or Tombs of Amascut while you have an Escape Crystal in your inventory will now consume the crystal and teleport you outside of the raid on login, preserving any HCIM status you might have.
* Aggie in Draynor Village has been updated with a Make-All interface for her red, yellow and blue dyes. Instead of crafting dyes one at a time through dialogue, you can now quickly select how many you’d like to make in one go.
* Lore books in Chambers and TOB will no longer drop once a player has read them.
* Fixed an issue where getting hit by another player's 'Duel' operation while using Mystic Cards would cause Emote 'Loop' options to stop working until the player moved tiles.
* The Alchemist's Amulet can no longer be purchased when the player has no space in their inventory.
* Fixed an issue where quickly destroying the Orb of Oculus while activating the Scry function could crash the client.
* Getting saved by a Phoenix necklace no longer restores your sanity in a Whisperer fight.

'''PvP Rota'''
The PvP rota has moved to '''Period B''':

* 560 - (UK) - PvP World
* 319 - (US) - Bounty Hunter World
* 579 - (US) - High-Risk PvP World
* 561 - (UK) - Free-to-Play PvP World
* 580 - (US) - LMS Competitive

World 390 (AUS) for LMS Competitive has been <u>'''de-activated'''</u> with this rota.

World 569 (AUS) for Bounty Hunter has been <u>'''de-activated'''</u> with this rota.

The PvP Arena is using '<b>Zerker</b>' loadouts in Ranked Duels and Tournaments this week.

